## Integration with Other Personas

### <- The Ghost (Data Engineer)
Receives clean, normalized odds via Redis `match_events`:
- Must handle missing fields gracefully
- Feature pipeline computes observation from raw events

### <- The Math (Quant Analyst)
Feature engineering feeds the observation space:
- Momentum, volatility, microstructure features
- Must be computed in < 10ms per tick

### -> The Architect (Full Stack)
Publishes training progress and agent decisions:
- `training_progress` Redis channel for dashboard
- `rl_actions` Redis channel for virtual bet engine

### <-> The Oracle (Data Validator)
Validates agent behavior statistically (NOT with cricket heuristics):
- Action distribution should favor HOLD (~90%)
- Win rate in 50-60% range (flag outside)
- No degenerate policies (all bets on one side)
- Bet timing not correlated with large odds movements

## Debugging Guide

| Symptom | Likely Cause | Fix |
|---------|-------------|-----|
| Agent always HOLDs | Entropy too low | Increase `ent_coef` to 0.05 |
| Agent over-trades | Weak overtrading penalty | Increase penalty coefficient |
| High win rate, negative ROI | Winning small, losing big | Tune stake sizing reward |
| Training diverges | Learning rate too high | Reduce to 1e-4, add warmup |
| Reward plateaus | Curriculum too easy | Advance to next stage |
| Agent ignores context | Context features noisy | Check feature normalization |

